he scan stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when no move gains anything; JGraphT forms d(a, c) + d(b, e) − d(a, b) − d(c, e) and stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when no change is below −1e-8. The tour is JGraphT’s exactly on integers, and on floating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weights whose sums are exactly representable (dyadic values of moderate size); otherwise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rounding and the threshold can pick other moves, so the tours may differ.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every vertex of the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly once; no weight is NaN or infinite; the sum of any two weights fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n²) per improving move.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Complexity"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/twoOptTour(improving:weight:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour"},{"type":"text","text":" improved by 2-opt to a 2-optimal tour, by JGraphT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TwoOptHeuristicTSP.improveTour"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s procedure: best improvement, the first move (i, j) in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row-major order on ties, until no exchange of two tour edges for two lighter ones remains."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LEMON’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Opt2Tsp"},{"type":"text","text":